(window.LMP_I18N = window.LMP_I18N || {})["en"] = {"cap.think":"Thinking","cap.think.body":"Reasons step by step before it answers. Better at math, logic and planning — you can read its thoughts.","cap.tools":"Tools","cap.tools.body":"Can run JavaScript, search the web or read a page in the middle of a reply — only if you turn tools on.","cap.vision":"Vision","cap.vision.body":"Understands photos. A small image add-on downloads with the model automatically.","card.branch":"<b>Change your mind.</b> Edit a message, regenerate a reply, or branch into a new chat without starting over.","card.branch.a1":"Maple leaves let go…","card.branch.a2":"Cold rain on the pond…","card.branch.q":"Write a haiku about autumn.","card.branch.tag":"↳ Branched into a new chat","card.docs":"<b>Ask your files.</b> PDF, Word, EPUB or Markdown — searched by meaning, answered from the right passages.","card.docs.a":"With <b>60 days’ written notice</b>, after the initial six months. <span class=\"muted\">— Section 8</span>","card.docs.indexed":"indexed","card.docs.q":"When can I terminate my lease?","card.prompts":"<b>Set the role once.</b> Save system prompts — a persona, a tone, a format — and reuse them with any model.","card.prompts.p1":"Concise · reply in French","card.prompts.p2":"Senior Kotlin reviewer","card.prompts.p3":"Explain like I'm five","card.tools":"<b>Let it take action.</b> Capable models can run JavaScript, search the web or read a page mid-reply.","card.tools.off":"Off by default","card.tools.results":"5 results","card.vision":"<b>Show it a photo.</b> Snap or pick an image and ask about it — read text, describe a scene, identify objects.","card.vision.a":"A fluffy sheep grazing in a green pasture on a sunny day.","card.vision.alt":"A sheep grazing in a field","card.voice":"<b>Speak instead of typing.</b> Words appear while you talk, in 35 languages. Recognition runs offline.","card.voice.q":"Plan a three-day trip to Lisbon with good coffee and…","control.body1":"<b>Drag the slider and watch the answer change.</b> Temperature decides how adventurous the model is — low for facts and code, high for brainstorming.","control.body2":"Top‑P, Top‑K, Min‑P, repetition penalty, seed and context size are all there too, and each model remembers its own settings.","control.eyebrow":"Control","control.title":"Dial in the personality.","cta.body":"Seconds to install. Minutes to download a model. Then you're done with the cloud.","cta.source":"Read the source on GitHub","cta.title":"Any model.<br/>In your pocket.","faq.a1":"LM Playground lets you run large language models directly on your Android device, iPhone or iPad. All processing happens locally – no cloud servers needed.","faq.a10":"**iPhone & iPad:** Go to Settings, then Models. Swipe left on a downloaded model and tap Delete.\n**Android:** Go to Settings, then Models. In the “Downloaded” section, tap the delete icon next to the model you want to remove.","faq.a11":"A system prompt is a reusable instruction that shapes how the model responds — for example, “You are a concise science tutor. Explain ideas clearly with everyday examples” or “You are a senior code reviewer. Point out bugs, edge cases, and security issues.” Create and manage them in Settings → System Prompts, then apply one to your chat. They are stored on your device and sent only to the local model.","faq.a12":"Tools let capable models take actions during a reply. Three are available: Run JavaScript (math, dates, and text processing in an on-device sandbox), Web search (finds current information on the web), and Fetch web page (reads a page so the model can summarize or quote it). Turn them on in Settings → Tools. Each is off by default and works only with models that support tool calling — look for the hammer badge in the model selector.","faq.a13":"Only when you enable them. Web search sends the model's query to DuckDuckGo, and Fetch web page downloads the pages the model chooses to open — those requests go to the websites themselves, not to the developer. Run JavaScript stays entirely on your device with no internet access. With every tool off (the default), nothing leaves your device. See the Privacy Policy for details.","faq.a14":"**iPhone & iPad:** No. iOS doesn't let apps use the GPU in the background, so a reply stops when you switch away. What was written so far is kept, and a Continue button finishes it when you come back.\n**Android:** Yes. While the app is in the background, a notification tracks the model's status — loaded, generating, then response ready — and lets you copy or share the reply. You can also enable a short completion chime in Settings → Sound and Haptic. Model downloads show their own progress notification with speed and ETA.","faq.a15":"No. Tap the microphone in the chat input and speak — a speech-recognition model turns your words into text on your phone as you talk, in 35 languages. The audio is never saved or sent anywhere, so dictation works fully offline. The model (718 MB) downloads once, the first time you use the microphone.","faq.a2":"The app supports models in GGUF format with Q4_K_M quantization, including Qwen 3, Gemma 3, Llama 3.2, Phi‑4 mini, and DeepSeek R1 Distill in various sizes.","faq.a3":"Model sizes vary from about 500 MB (small models like Qwen 3 0.6B) to several GB (larger models like DeepSeek R1 7B). Make sure you have enough free space before downloading.","faq.a4":"Internet is needed to download models, and — if you turn them on — for the optional web tools (web search and fetch page). Apart from that, once a model is downloaded it runs completely offline on your device.","faq.a5":"Your conversations are processed locally on your device and are never sent to a server by the app. The one exception is the optional web tools: if you enable web search or fetch page, the model's search queries and the pages it opens are sent to those websites (search uses DuckDuckGo). Tools are off by default, so nothing leaves your device unless you turn them on. See the Privacy Policy for details.","faq.a6":"Larger models take more time to load into memory. Loading times depend on your device's hardware. Once loaded, the model stays in memory until you unload it.","faq.a7":"Devices with more RAM can run larger models. For best performance, use a device with at least 6 GB of RAM for small models and 8+ GB for larger ones.","faq.a8":"**iPhone & iPad:** Yes. In Settings → Models, tap Import and choose a .gguf file, or copy it into the Models folder of LM Playground in the Files app. The app picks it up automatically and shows it alongside the built-in catalog. Chat template and tokenizer settings are read from the GGUF metadata. If a specific model doesn't work, please open an issue on GitHub.\n**Android:** Yes. Place your .gguf file in the storage folder selected in Settings → Models (the same folder used for downloads). The app will pick it up automatically and show it in the model selector alongside the built-in catalog. Chat template and tokenizer settings are read from the GGUF metadata. If a specific model doesn't work, please open an issue on GitHub.","faq.a9":"**iPhone & iPad:** In the Models folder of LM Playground, which you can see in the Files app and in Finder when your device is connected to a Mac.\n**Android:** Yes. Go to Settings, then Models, and use the “Change Folder” option to select a different storage location.","faq.eyebrow":"FAQ","faq.ios.a":"Coming soon to the App Store. LM Playground for iOS will need iOS 26 or later and an iPhone 15 Pro or newer, or an iPad with an M1 chip or newer. Chat, vision, documents, dictation and tools all run on your device, just as they do on Android.","faq.ios.q":"Is LM Playground available on iPhone and iPad?","faq.q1":"What is LM Playground?","faq.q10":"How do I delete a model?","faq.q11":"What are system prompts?","faq.q12":"What are tools and which ones are available?","faq.q13":"Do the web tools send my data online?","faq.q14":"Will the app notify me when a response is ready?","faq.q15":"Does voice dictation send my voice anywhere?","faq.q2":"What models are supported?","faq.q3":"How much storage space do I need?","faq.q4":"Does the app require an internet connection?","faq.q5":"Is my data private?","faq.q6":"Why is model loading slow?","faq.q7":"Which devices work best?","faq.q8":"Can I load a custom GGUF model?","faq.q9":"Can I change where models are stored?","faq.sub":"Still stuck? Open an issue on GitHub or reach out directly.","faq.title":"Questions you had<br/>before you asked.","features.lead":"Chat, vision, documents, voice and tools — <b>all running on the chip in your pocket.</b>","features.title":"Everything you expect.<br/>Nothing that leaves.","flow.a1":"15% of 240 is <b>36</b>.","flow.a2":"また明日 — <i>mata ashita</i>.","flow.a3":"Thursday’s sync moves to Friday at 10am.","flow.a4":"No — 391 = <b>17 × 23</b>.","flow.q1":"What’s 15% of 240?","flow.q2":"Translate “see you tomorrow” into Japanese.","flow.q3":"Summarize this email in one line.","flow.q4":"Is 391 a prime number?","footer.about":"Open-source app for running large language models locally on iPhone and iPad (coming soon) and Android. Built on <a href=\"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp\">llama.cpp</a>. MIT licensed.","footer.build":"Build","footer.build.issues":"Issue tracker","footer.build.releases":"Releases","footer.contact":"Contact","footer.email":"Email","footer.privacy":"Privacy Policy","footer.product":"Product","footer.product.models":"All models","hero.cta.android":"Get it on Google Play","hero.cta.ios":"App Store · Soon","hero.lead":"Run large language models <b>completely offline</b>. No cloud, no account, no tracking — free and open source.","hero.note":"iPhone 15 Pro+ and M1+ iPad · Android 11+ · MIT licensed","hero.publishers":"Runs open-weight models from","hero.title":"Private AI.<br/>Right on your phone.","how.dl.choose":"Choose a model","how.dl.downloading":"Downloading · Wi‑Fi","how.dl.eta":"{speed} MB/s · {time} left","how.dl.ready":"✓ Ready to chat","how.dl.saved":"Saved on device","how.dl.wait":"Waiting…","how.dl.waiting":"Waiting for a tap","how.eyebrow":"How it works","how.lead":"Tap a model to try it — <b>or just watch.</b>","how.s1.body":"Choose from 40 open models, or bring your own GGUF.","how.s1.title":"Pick a model","how.s2.body":"Background downloads with progress and automatic resume.","how.s2.title":"Download once","how.s3.body":"Reasoning shown inline. History stays on your device.","how.s3.title":"Chat offline","how.title":"Three taps to your<br/>first token.","lang.body":"The whole app is translated into 28 languages, and on first launch it suggests a model that speaks yours. <a class=\"link\" href=\"https://github.com/andriydruk/LMPlayground\">Improve a translation</a>","lang.eyebrow":"Languages","lang.title":"Speaks your language.","meta.title":"LM Playground — Private AI on your phone","models.browse":"Browse all models","models.byo":"Want something specific? <b>Bring your own GGUF</b> — the app reads the chat template from the file.","models.eyebrow":"Models","models.lead":"A model is the AI behind the chat — <b>one file you download once.</b> Bigger models know more and reason better, but need more memory. Pick how much RAM your phone has to see good fits.","models.ram.note":"Picks are the most downloaded models that fit. iPhone 15 Pro and newer have 8 GB; on Android, look in Settings → About phone.","models.ram.q":"How much RAM does your phone have?","models.title":"Find the right brain<br/>for your phone.","mp.byo.android":"Put the .gguf file in the folder chosen in Settings → Models. It shows up next to the built-in models.","mp.byo.body":"The chat template and tokenizer are read straight from the file, so most GGUF models just work. If one doesn’t, <a class=\"link\" href=\"https://github.com/andriydruk/LMPlayground/issues\">tell us on GitHub</a>","mp.byo.chat":"Pick it from the model selector like any other model.","mp.byo.chat.title":"Start chatting","mp.byo.eyebrow":"Bring your own","mp.byo.ios":"Tap Import in Settings → Models, or copy the file into the app’s Models folder in Files.","mp.byo.ios.title":"iPhone and iPad","mp.byo.title":"Don’t see your favorite?<br/>Load any GGUF.","mp.count.models":"models","mp.count.publishers":"publishers","mp.count.tools":"can use tools","mp.count.vision":"see images","mp.downloads":"{n} downloads / month","mp.empty":"No models match. Try another filter — or bring your own GGUF.","mp.f.all":"All","mp.f.new":"New","mp.f.small":"Under 1 GB","mp.lead":"Open models picked and tuned for phones. <b>Each one runs entirely on your device</b> — download it once and it works offline from then on.","mp.meta.title":"Models — LM Playground","mp.search":"Search models","mp.shown.all":"Showing all {n} models","mp.shown.some":"Showing {n} of {total} models","mp.sort":"Sort models","mp.sort.large":"Largest first","mp.sort.name":"Name","mp.sort.new":"Newest first","mp.sort.popular":"Most popular","mp.sort.small":"Smallest first","mp.source":"Downloads are Hugging Face downloads of each model’s GGUF files over the last 30 days (checked November 21, 2026).","mp.title":"Every model.<br/>One tap away.","nav.download":"Download","nav.faq":"FAQ","nav.features":"Features","nav.how":"How it works","nav.models":"Models","nav.privacy":"Privacy","phone.a":"Machine learning is a branch of artificial intelligence where computers **learn from data** instead of being explicitly programmed.\n\nKey concepts:\n\n• **Training**: feeding data to algorithms\n• **Models**: learned patterns from data\n• **Inference**: making predictions on new data","phone.a1":"At 4% compounded annually, $5,000 grows to **$7,401.22** in 10 years — that is 5,000 × 1.04^10. So you would earn about **$2,401** in interest on top of your $5,000 principal.","phone.a2":"Reviewers are largely positive. The wins: a much brighter **3000-nit display**, about **20% better battery life**, and a sharper telephoto camera, plus faster on-device AI. The main gripe is the **higher starting price** — but most still call it the best Pixel yet.","phone.a3":"Karpathy proposes an **LLM-maintained wiki** — a persistent, cross-linked markdown layer the model builds between you and your raw sources. Rather than re-reading everything per query, it updates pages and links as new material arrives, so your knowledge base **compounds** instead of being re-derived each time.","phone.aD":"You can terminate with **60 days’ written notice** after the initial six-month period. Your deposit is returned within **14 days** of move-out (Section 8.2).","phone.aV":"A **sheep** with a thick, curly cream-white fleece, grazing head-down on a lush green hillside. The overcast sky and rocky pasture suggest a cool, upland setting.","phone.input":"Message","phone.q":"What is machine learning?","phone.q1":"If I invest $5,000 at 4% annual interest, what will it be worth in 10 years?","phone.q2":"What are reviewers saying about the latest Pixel?","phone.q3":"Summarize this article: https://gist.github.com/karpathy/442a6bf555914893e9891c11519de94f","phone.qD":"When can I terminate my rental agreement?","phone.qV":"What animal is in this photo?","phone.r0":"The user wants a simple definition. Cover learning from data versus explicit rules, then the core steps: training, models, and inference. Keep it beginner-friendly.","phone.r1":"Future value with compound interest: FV = P(1 + r)^n, with P = 5000, r = 0.04, n = 10. 1.04^10 is about 1.4802, so FV is about 7401.22. Interest = FV − P, about 2401.","phone.r2":"The results agree on display, battery, and camera gains, plus faster on-device AI. The recurring negative is the higher price. Summarize as praise versus the main drawback.","phone.r3":"Karpathy proposes an LLM-maintained personal wiki. Three layers: immutable raw sources, an LLM-generated wiki, and a schema file. The model updates pages and cross-links as new sources arrive, so knowledge compounds. Summarize the idea and the layering.","phone.rD":"The excerpts say the lease can be ended after the initial six-month term with 60 days’ written notice, and Section 8.2 covers the deposit: returned within 14 days of move-out. Answer with both.","phone.rV":"The user wants me to identify the animal in the photo. It is a woolly sheep grazing head-down on a green hillside. Answer briefly and note its key features.","phone.send":"Send","phone.tD":"Searching document","phone.thinking":"Thinking","priv.airplane":"Airplane mode","priv.body1":"<b>Pull the SIM. Turn off Wi‑Fi. Keep chatting.</b> Once a model is downloaded, inference happens entirely on your phone — on a flight, in the subway, anywhere.","priv.body2":"No account, no API keys, no telemetry, no analytics. Web tools are optional and off by default.","priv.eyebrow":"Privacy","priv.legend.net":"Network traffic","priv.legend.tokens":"Tokens on your phone","priv.link":"Read the privacy policy","priv.sent":"sent over the network","priv.title":"Private by construction.","priv.tokens":"tokens generated","priv.wifi":"Wi‑Fi off","privacy.contact_label":"Contact","privacy.date":"Effective Date: June 2, 2026","privacy.intro":"Welcome to LM Playground! I am committed to maintaining the trust and confidence of everyone who uses my app. This Privacy Policy explains what the app does and does not collect, how your conversations stay on your device, and the few cases — such as the optional web tools — where information leaves your device, so you always know what to expect.","privacy.s1.body":"I, Andriy Druk, the developer of LM Playground, do not collect, store, use, or share any personal information from the users of my app. There are no accounts, no advertising, and no usage analytics or tracking. The app is designed with your privacy as a priority, so you can use it without compromising your personal data.","privacy.s1.title":"1. No Personal Information Collection","privacy.s2.body":"Your conversations, system prompts, and the model's responses are processed locally on your device by the on-device model. This content is never sent to me or to any server for inference. It stays on your device unless you choose to use a feature that reaches the internet, as described below.","privacy.s2.title":"2. On-Device Processing","privacy.s3.body":"LM Playground connects to the internet for two purposes: to download the model files you choose, and — only if you turn them on — to power the optional web tools. The app contains no advertising, telemetry, or usage analytics, and it does not report your activity back to me.","privacy.s3.title":"3. Internet Access","privacy.s4.body":"Capable models can use optional tools, which are turned off by default. When you enable the web tools, some information leaves your device: the Web search tool sends the model's search query to DuckDuckGo, and the Fetch web page tool downloads the pages the model decides to open from those websites. Those requests are handled by the third-party sites under their own privacy policies — I neither receive nor store them. The Run JavaScript tool runs entirely on your device in a sandbox with no internet access. To keep everything offline, simply leave the tools off.","privacy.s4.title":"4. Tools and Web Access","privacy.s5.body":"As the developer of LM Playground, I reserve the right to update this Privacy Policy at any time. Any changes will be effective immediately upon posting the updated policy. Users are encouraged to review this page periodically and stay informed about how their privacy is protected.","privacy.s5.title":"5. Privacy Policy Updates","privacy.s6.body":"By using LM Playground, you acknowledge and agree to this Privacy Policy. If you do not agree with the policy, please refrain from using the app. Your continued use of the app following the posting of any updates or changes to this policy will be deemed your acceptance of those changes.","privacy.s6.title":"6. Acceptance of This Policy","privacy.s7.body":"If you have any questions or suggestions about my Privacy Policy, do not hesitate to contact me.","privacy.s7.title":"7. Contact Me","privacy.title":"Privacy Policy","prompts.new":"New system prompt","qa.stuck":"Still stuck? <a class=\"link\" href=\"https://github.com/andriydruk/LMPlayground/issues\">Open an issue on GitHub</a>","qa.title":"Questions?<br/>Answers.","store.android.small":"GET IT ON","store.ios.small":"COMING SOON ON THE","tools.t1.title":"Run JavaScript","tools.t2.title":"Web search","tools.t3.title":"Fetch web page","tp.balanced":"Balanced","tp.context":"Context 4,096","tp.creative":"Creative","tp.focused":"Focused","tp.o1":"Ocean Blue.","tp.o2":"Harbor Mist — a soft, cool gray-blue.","tp.o3":"Midnight Orchard: deep plum with a hint of green.","tp.o4":"Thunderstorm Lavender, flecked with copper like rain on a tin roof.","tp.o5":"Velvet Static — the color a radio hums at 3 a.m. when nobody is listening.","tp.precise":"Precise","tp.q":"Name a new paint color.","tp.repeat":"Repeat penalty 1.1","tp.seed":"Seed","tp.surprising":"Surprising","tp.temperature":"Temperature","tp.wild":"Wild","ui.next":"Next","ui.prev":"Previous","ui.theme":"Toggle light or dark theme","units.tokens":"%d tokens","why.devices.body":"iPhone 15 Pro and newer and M1 iPads are coming soon. Android 11 and newer works today.","why.devices.ipad":"iPad · soon","why.devices.iphone":"iPhone · soon","why.devices.title":"iPhone, iPad and Android.","why.engine.body":"The open-source engine behind local AI. Bring any GGUF file and it just works.","why.engine.title":"Powered by llama.cpp.","why.free.body":"No subscription, no account, no ads. Every line of code is on GitHub.","why.free.title":"Free. For good.","why.size.body":"Forty open models, from tiny ones that fit any phone to reasoning giants for flagships. Every dot below is a model you can download.","why.size.title":"From 267 MB to 12 GB.","why.speed.body":"GPU-accelerated with Metal on iPhone and iPad, and Vulkan on Android.","why.speed.title":"Answers stream in as it thinks.","why.title":"Small enough for your pocket.<br/>Smart enough to matter."};
